  "home": "<div class=\"strata-tutorial-index\"></div>\n<h1 class=\"wp-block-heading\" id=\"tutorials\">Tutorials <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#tutorials\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h1>\n<p class=\"tagline\">Step-by-step walkthroughs for building scenes, games, animation and characters with Strata — by hand, no AI required. <span id=\"count\">28 tutorials.</span></p>\n<div class=\"jump\" id=\"jump\" aria-label=\"Sections\">&#10;\t\t&#10;\t\t<a href=\"#scenes\">Scenes<span class=\"n\">8</span></a>&#10;\t\t<a href=\"#games\">Games<span class=\"n\">4</span></a>&#10;\t\t<a href=\"#animation-and-rendering\">Animation and rendering<span class=\"n\">8</span></a>&#10;\t\t<a href=\"#characters\">Characters<span class=\"n\">5</span></a>&#10;\t\t<a href=\"#motion-capture\">Motion capture<span class=\"n\">3</span></a>&#10;\t\t&#10;\t</div>\n<div id=\"list\">&#10;\t\t&#10;\t\t<section>&#10;\t\t\t<h2 id=\"scenes\">Scenes <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#scenes\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>&#10;\t\t\t<p class=\"note\">Build and label a scene, or cut a model into named parts.</p>&#10;\t\t\t<div class=\"grid\">&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/gis-walkway-shade.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/gis-walkway-shade.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"build-a-gis-grounded-scene-by-hand\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/gis-walkway-shade.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build a GIS-grounded scene by hand</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#build-a-gis-grounded-scene-by-hand\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Build a Mesa site scene from mapped paths and a footprint without AI, add procedural finishes and cinematic lighting, and verify every saved result. AI assistance remains optional and human-checked.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1&amp;file=flux.json&amp;commit=7b9359e3b2226064e9852cbce5d2c721175957a1&amp;play=false\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"futureflux-from-a-mesa-heat-map-to-a-tree-shade-proposal\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/futureflux-mesa.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">FutureFlux: From a Mesa heat map to a tree-shade proposal</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#futureflux-from-a-mesa-heat-map-to-a-tree-shade-proposal\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Follow a bilingual Mesa surface-heat tour, then use a Playwright harness to test how suggestions are clarified, reviewed, and turned into scene edits.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/segment-any-mesh.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/segment-any-mesh.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"cut-any-textured-mesh-into-named-parts\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/segment-any-mesh.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cut any textured mesh into named parts</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#cut-any-textured-mesh-into-named-parts\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>The editor&#39;s SEG tool on any one-piece textured model: read the UV islands and painted colours, decide what each piece is, and cut it into named, classed meshes in one undo step. An avocado is the easy case, a toy duck the hard one (ten islands, six parts), an animated fox shows a skinned mesh cut with its skeleton and clips intact, and the page says where the method stops working. Built with the JS Shell.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1@554a8ee2f39a1fe1b1ebe56208fd382b3bbef8e1&amp;file=duck.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/segment-a-scene.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/segment-a-scene.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"cut-a-scene-into-named-parts\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/segment-a-scene.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cut a scene into named parts</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#cut-a-scene-into-named-parts\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>SEG on a furnished room: one mesh, 538 texture islands, no part that is one island. SEG joins the islands that touch into components, measures them in the world frame, places everything you did not name on the nearest anchor you did, and checks the cut; you supply the anchors and their names. Says where the checks fired on the first attempt. Built with the JS Shell.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/segment-a-diorama.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/segment-a-diorama.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"name-every-part-of-a-street-corner-diorama\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/segment-a-diorama.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Name every part of a street-corner diorama</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#name-every-part-of-a-street-corner-diorama\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>SEG on a 71-mesh street-corner diorama whose biggest mesh has 3,297 texture islands: too many to anchor individually. An agent names 22 regions from orthographic views, cuts nine meshes into 124 named, classed parts, names the 62 meshes that were already separate, and selects one object across all its materials with a class. Says where SEG&#39;s own warning caught a second post box, and that the cut replays. Built with the JS Shell.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1@3c4520491a63c23ac02366bfe2b79da2cab41cb8&amp;file=littletokyo.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/segment-a-mesh.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/segment-a-mesh.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"cut-an-avocado-into-named-parts-building-the-tool-by-hand\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/segment-a-mesh.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Cut an avocado into named parts, building the tool by hand</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#cut-an-avocado-into-named-parts-building-the-tool-by-hand\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>The editor&#39;s SEG tool, written out by hand on a one-piece avocado: read the evidence the file carries (separate patches of the texture, and the colours painted on them), cut it into five named, classed meshes (skin, pit, cavity, flesh, edge) without losing a triangle, and check the cut. Says plainly where the method stops working. Built with the JS Shell.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1@554a8ee2f39a1fe1b1ebe56208fd382b3bbef8e1&amp;file=avocado.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/build-a-scene.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/build-a-scene.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"build-a-night-scene-from-scratch\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/build-a-scene.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build a night scene from scratch</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#build-a-night-scene-from-scratch\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>The from-scratch workflow: helper functions, noise-displaced ground, night lighting, a moving object and a hero camera.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1&amp;file=bus-stop.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/wizard-hat-sculpt.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/wizard-hat-sculpt.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"build-a-wizard-hat-and-sculpt-a-face-into-it\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/wizard-hat-sculpt.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build a wizard hat and sculpt a face into it</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#build-a-wizard-hat-and-sculpt-a-face-into-it\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Assemble a hat from primitives, then sculpt a relief smiley into it as one undoable step.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t</section>&#10;\t\t<section>&#10;\t\t\t<h2 id=\"games\">Games <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#games\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>&#10;\t\t\t<p class=\"note\">Build a scene, label it, and leave the behaviour to game code.</p>&#10;\t\t\t<div class=\"grid\">&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/paddle-table-view.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/paddle-table-view.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"build-a-table-view-paddle-game-scene\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/paddle-table-view.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build a table-view paddle game scene</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#build-a-table-view-paddle-game-scene\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Build a paddle game as a receding table, and verify the camera framing by projecting points to screen space.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/bubble-shooter-scene.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/bubble-shooter-scene.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"build-a-bubble-shooter-scene\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/bubble-shooter-scene.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build a bubble shooter scene</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#build-a-bubble-shooter-scene\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>A lane, one class-tagged bubble template for game code to clone, a rainforest backdrop and a score sign.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/fight-arena-scene.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/fight-arena-scene.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"build-a-fighting-game-arena-scene\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/fight-arena-scene.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build a fighting-game arena scene</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#build-a-fighting-game-arena-scene\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>A tavern stage, two class-tagged fighters and a health-and-mana HUD, built for game code to drive.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/racing-circuit-scene.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/racing-circuit-scene.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"build-a-labelled-racing-circuit-with-a-script\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/racing-circuit-scene.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build a labelled racing circuit with a script</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#build-a-labelled-racing-circuit-with-a-script\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Generate a whole circuit from corner points and name every object at creation so game engines can find it.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t</section>&#10;\t\t<section>&#10;\t\t\t<h2 id=\"animation-and-rendering\">Animation and rendering <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#animation-and-rendering\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>&#10;\t\t\t<p class=\"note\">Timelines, cameras and shots.</p>&#10;\t\t\t<div class=\"grid\">&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/makeshort.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/makeshort.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"make-a-pythagorean-theorem-short\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/makeshort.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Make a Pythagorean-theorem short</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#make-a-pythagorean-theorem-short\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Build a 100-second animated demonstration that 3² + 4² = 5², extend it to two more triples with quarter turns of the camera, and add subtitles, using the JS Shell and the Universal Timeline.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1&amp;file=pyth.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/a-plus-b-cubed.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/a-plus-b-cubed.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"build-the-a-b-3-proof-in-3d\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/a-plus-b-cubed.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Build the (a + b)³ proof in 3D</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#build-the-a-b-3-proof-in-3d\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>A 3D visual proof of (a + b)³ = a³ + 3a²b + 3ab² + b³ with no numbers: a whole cube falls apart into eight coloured blocks that line up under the expanded equation, with five cameras, an x-ray and subtitles, all from the JS Shell.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1&amp;file=a%2Bb-cubed.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/hardy-weinberg.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/hw.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"hardy-weinberg-as-a-square\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/hardy-weinberg.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hardy–Weinberg as a square</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#hardy-weinberg-as-a-square\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>The Hardy–Weinberg law as a square: p² + 2pq + q² for one round of random mating, then a count of the alleles that shows p and q are unchanged, with the assumptions listed. Built with the JS Shell.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1@89f9272c7b891ab7bf798a2b58de4b3a08a36eab&amp;file=hw.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/area-volume.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/area-volume.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"why-cells-are-small-surface-area-to-volume\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/area-volume.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Why cells are small: surface area to volume</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#why-cells-are-small-surface-area-to-volume\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Cubes of side 1, 2 and 3 have surface-to-volume ratios of 6, 3 and 2 per unit-cube width, falling as 1 / side in any units: why cells stay small and divide, and why mitochondria and lungs fold their membranes. Built with the JS Shell.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1@89f9272c7b891ab7bf798a2b58de4b3a08a36eab&amp;file=area-volume.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/projectile.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/projectile.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"a-projectile-two-motions-one-path\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/projectile.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">A projectile: two motions, one path</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#a-projectile-two-motions-one-path\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>A thrown ball&#39;s curve is a sideways motion at constant speed plus an up-and-down motion under gravity. Orbit the path to see each alone, then put them back together. Built with the JS Shell.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1@3bd6749e4d9d28a292160ce9d5d543df2447dc75&amp;file=projectile.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/piston.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/piston.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"a-crank-a-rod-and-a-piston-crank-slider-kinematics\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/piston.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">A crank, a rod and a piston: crank-slider kinematics</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#a-crank-a-rod-and-a-piston-crank-slider-kinematics\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>A crankshaft, connecting rod and piston through one revolution: the dead centers, the stroke, and the mechanical advantage drawn as a gap that vanishes at the dead centers. Orbit the assembly to see what a flat view hides. Built with the JS Shell.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1@cf7be14bd7500edb71ad94b5b886351627f5fe05&amp;file=piston.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/molecule-shapes.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/molecule-shapes.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"why-molecules-are-shaped-differently-electron-pair-repulsion\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/molecule-shapes.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Why molecules are shaped differently: electron-pair repulsion</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#why-molecules-are-shaped-differently-electron-pair-repulsion\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Methane, ammonia and water built from coloured spheres and bonds: four electron pairs spread to the corners of a tetrahedron, and each lone pair, which has no atom on it, closes the angle a little more (109.5°, 107°, 104.5°). Orbit each molecule to see what a flat drawing hides. Built with the JS Shell.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1@e223905dc246ba30bbd233662240a0f6d6f53d9b&amp;file=molecule-shapes.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/render-camera-sequence.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/render-camera-sequence.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"add-a-static-hero-camera-to-a-render-sequence\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/render-camera-sequence.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Add a static hero camera to a render sequence</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#add-a-static-hero-camera-to-a-render-sequence\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Cut a fixed hero camera into a render sequence to show a moment your main camera does not frame well.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t</section>&#10;\t\t<section>&#10;\t\t\t<h2 id=\"characters\">Characters <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#characters\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>&#10;\t\t\t<p class=\"note\">Import, restyle, pose and animate a character.</p>&#10;\t\t\t<div class=\"grid\">&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/make-your-own-metahuman.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/make-your-own-metahuman.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"make-your-own-metahuman\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/make-your-own-metahuman.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Make your own MetaHuman</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#make-your-own-metahuman\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Import a MetaHuman GLB, restyle it, pose its 51 face blendshapes and capture a still.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/two-character-dance.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/two-character-dance.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"one-dance-two-characters\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/two-character-dance.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">One dance, two characters</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#one-dance-two-characters\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Bake one Mixamo dance onto two different characters and stage them with an orbiting camera.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/vrm-restyle-explorer.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/vrm-restyle-explorer.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"restyle-a-vrm-into-an-explorer-with-the-js-shell\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/vrm-restyle-explorer.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Restyle a VRM into an explorer with the JS Shell</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#restyle-a-vrm-into-an-explorer-with-the-js-shell\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Restyle a VRoid base model into an expedition explorer: retint, re-clothe, attach gear and pose a smirk.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/animate-a-character.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/animate-a-character.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"animate-a-finished-character-clips-a-timeline-and-a-camera\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/animate-a-character.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Animate a finished character: clips, a timeline and a camera</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#animate-a-finished-character-clips-a-timeline-and-a-camera\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Open a finished VRM that carries a baked body clip and a baked face clip, read what the file holds, start the body on cue and keep a camera on her as she walks. Character by portrait.webcli.app and look.webcli.app, rigged with rig.webcli.app.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<a class=\"try\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/#repo=tejaswigowda/test1@543069a031abcea1ce4103a82710ee1845efa019&amp;file=facebind.json&amp;present=true\" title=\"Open the finished scene in the editor\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Open example →</a>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/author-a-face.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/author-a-face.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"authoring-a-face-gaze-and-idle\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/author-a-face.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Authoring a face: gaze and idle</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#authoring-a-face-gaze-and-idle\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Give two characters a face with timeline keys: gaze that follows, a seeded blink and held expressions.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t</section>&#10;\t\t<section>&#10;\t\t\t<h2 id=\"motion-capture\">Motion capture <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#motion-capture\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h2>&#10;\t\t\t<p class=\"note\">Work from recorded performances.</p>&#10;\t\t\t<div class=\"grid\">&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/martial-arts-dojo.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/martial-arts-dojo.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"a-martial-arts-lesson-then-a-sparring-match-in-a-bamboo-dojo\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/martial-arts-dojo.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">A martial-arts lesson, then a sparring match, in a bamboo dojo</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#a-martial-arts-lesson-then-a-sparring-match-in-a-bamboo-dojo\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Two characters share one mocap clip in a bamboo dojo: a lesson, then a sparring match filmed by four cameras.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/edit-captured-motion.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/edit-captured-motion.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"editing-captured-motion-as-data\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/edit-captured-motion.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Editing captured motion as data</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#editing-captured-motion-as-data\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Cut a 170-second two-performer capture to 53 seconds with a non-destructive edit list.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t<article class=\"card\">&#10;\t\t\t\t<a class=\"thumb\" href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/sparring-from-mocap.html\" aria-hidden=\"true\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/screenshots/thumbs/sparring-from-mocap.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"640\" height=\"400\" loading=\"lazy\"></a>&#10;\t\t\t\t<div class=\"body\">&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<h3 id=\"a-sparring-match-from-a-two-person-motion-capture\"><a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/tutorials/sparring-from-mocap.html\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">A sparring match from a two-person motion capture</a> <a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#a-sparring-match-from-a-two-person-motion-capture\" aria-label=\"Link to this section\">#</a></h3>&#10;\t\t\t\t\t<p>Turn a two-person sparring capture into a 53-second match, checked frame by frame for collisions.</p>&#10;\t\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t\t</article>&#10;\t\t\t</div>&#10;\t\t</section>&#10;\t\t&#10;\t</div>\n<div class=\"tutorial-footer\">&#10;\t\t<a href=\"https://strataeditor.dev/about/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">← Back to about</a>&#10;\t</div>"
}
